	- hear the tune to check that it is right and adjust the tempo.
	- the book writes F#7, B7 and E7 as (alt); they are written here as 7.5+.9+.
	- bars 1-4, 6 and 9: the fast triplet lines are hard to read in the handwritten scan, check every note and accidental against a recording.
	- bars 1 and 3: the naturals in the second triplet were read as E naturals (the heads sit between E and F).
	- bar 6: the last note may be a G rather than an F.
	- bar 11: the triplet may be E G A rather than E F A.
	- interlude: the book writes '(Fine)' under the first Bb7 bar; it is put on that bar here.
	REMARKS:
	- the interlude is played in even eighths. Solos are on the head changes and the interlude is played between the soloists.
